    {
      "caption": "A common mistake: moving a vector changes it",
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "id": "s5",
      "narration":"A common mistake: moving a vector changes it: position vectors are pinned to the origin, so every vector feels pinned. Free vectors slide: the same arrow drawn anywhere is the same vector. Only position vectors are pinned to the origin. Dot product is the two lengths times cos theta; a line is r equals a plus lambda b.",
